{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454935-methuselahs-in-the-new-world","id":1454935,"title":"Methuselahs in the New World","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-14T20:00:12-07:00","id":1454935,"title":"Methuselahs in the New World","content":"Something that's always bugged me. What were Methuselahs doing in the New World so early anyways? Menele, The Wanderer, whoever is responsible for the Tlacique...all long before anyone had any right to be there (outside of maybe Drowned Legacies, and the indigenous population). Like Menele's story claims he did it to find a place where Helena couldn't find him, but given how dangerous those early sea voyages would be (not going to discuss Finnegan's Flight, that's just ridiculous), it really seems strange that old vampires would just randomly decide, hey, let's go see if there's another continent out there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-14T21:32:26-07:00","id":1454941,"title":"","content":"The Wanderer, assuming you mean Mictlantecuhtli, was indigenous, so it's more a question of how/why his sire was in the Americas. A Gangrel Methuselah is probably the best equipped to make such a journey on their own (assuming they actually are Gangrel).<br /> <br /> In Menele's case, my understanding is that he took the journey with no question &quot;if&quot; there was another continent (I thought he knew due to advanced Auspex, but wiki says he was motivated by ancient legends, which does seem a bit sketchier). A journey that might be dangerous for mortals would probably be less so for a Methuselah in possession of advanced Thaumaturgy.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-14T21:41:08-07:00","id":1454943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lynceus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454935-methuselahs-in-the-new-world#post1454935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something that's always bugged me. What were Methuselahs doing in the New World so early anyways? Menele, The Wanderer, whoever is responsible for the Tlacique...all long before anyone had any right to be there (outside of maybe Drowned Legacies, and the indigenous population). Like Menele's story claims he did it to find a place where Helena couldn't find him, but given how dangerous those early sea voyages would be (not going to discuss Finnegan's Flight, that's just ridiculous), it really seems strange that old vampires would just randomly decide, hey, let's go see if there's another continent out there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh well, Kharnov finished first, but here it goes anyway.<br /> <br /> <br /> - Menele, according to some bits in the backstory of Critias (who actually unknowingly enabled it), came to the Americas sometime in the 1200s-1300s, so before Columbus but definitely a few centuries after <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leif_Erikson\" target=\"_blank\">Leif Erikson</a>'s journeys &amp; discoveries. Same goes for <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Bjorn_Garinson\" target=\"_blank\">Bjorn Garinson</a>, the Brujah primogen in Washington DC, mostly.<br /> Also, i'm pretty sure CbN implies Menele already had some evidence such a land existed - from Auspex, from time-lost punic chronicles about accidental discovery by sailors following the african coast, or a combination of the two - before actually making the journey.<br /> <br /> <br /> - <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Mictlantecuhtli_(VTM)\" target=\"_blank\">The Wanderer</a>, if you check his backstory in Diablerie: Mexico, <b>is an actual native american</b> embraced in what would become British Columbia sometime in the 1st century AC. His <b>nameless sire</b> is the one with supposed old world (possibly roman or gallic origins, if a &quot;before Caesar crossed the Rubicon&quot; commentary serves as indication) origins and based on location, might have come <b><i>by foot</i></b> (or paw &amp; wing), crossing the Bering Strait.<br /> <br /> <br /> - The <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Tlacique\" target=\"_blank\">Tlacique</a> i know little to nothing about, but even their Wikia entry says their common origin is contentious and association might owe more to politics than actual blood relations, so everything should be taken with a grain of salt. <i>Specially </i>considering that two of their common disciplines are also shared with the Baali, that <b><a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Huitzilopochtli_(VTM)#God_of_the_Aztecs\" target=\"_blank\">definitely </a></b>had a pre-columbian presence in the region acording to the books (though even then some might be less reliable than others).<br /> And if their founder <b>was </b>indeed a rogue setite and not a rogue Baali or something else altogether - well, the Sahara is a fairly large place potentially bridging the space from Egypt to Atlantic seaboard in a way not unlike the Great Steppe/Silk Road did for lands between Europe and Southeast Asia.<br /> <br /> Just some thoughts, hope this helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-15-2021, 01:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-15T03:44:25-07:00","id":1454948,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, I vaguely recalled The Wanderer and thought that was <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:rubik\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Mictlantecuhtli's Sire, not the Methuselah himself, research fail (it was The Slumbering Giant). This is the first I heard that the Tlacique might be Baali instead of Followers/Ministry, but that's an interesting alternative to their origins. But if we're saying that since Critias is based on one of Plato's students, and the legend of Atlantis comes from the dialogues of Critias and Timaeus, wherein which Critias tells the tale of Solon's journey to Egypt (where Solon heard the tale of the lost continent), that Menele was searching for Atlantis...wow. With nothing more than the legend of a lost continent and a high level Auspex ability, he made his way to the New World That's kind of nuts, lol. But after some digging, there are unconfirmed theories that the Phoenicians made their way to the New World, so I guess that's not so farfetched. And if we are saying The Slumbering Giant came across the land bridge, what about the Nosferatu Methuselah that Mictlantecuhtli commited Diablerie upon? They must have found their way to South America in what, the 6th century? Who also, apparently, was fleeing the Jyhad. I don't know what's more amazing- that multiple 4th Generation vampires got the idea to head to the New World, or that they made it without going &quot;ah, you know what, this is a terrible idea&quot;.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-15T05:00:39-07:00","id":1454952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lynceus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454935-methuselahs-in-the-new-world?p=1454948#post1454948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah, I vaguely recalled The Wanderer and thought that was <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:rubik\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Mictlantecuhtli's Sire, not the Methuselah himself, research fail (it was The Slumbering Giant).</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:rubik\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">It happens.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lynceus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454935-methuselahs-in-the-new-world?p=1454948#post1454948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the first I heard that the Tlacique might be Baali instead of Followers/Ministry, but that's an interesting alternative to their origins.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing specifically calling out the Baali in the books per se, but overall the arguments in favor of Tlacique being setites - possessing Obfuscate &amp; Presence and founders that like to play (dark) god - are flimsy and just as applicable to them, so, my random alternate theory to mess things up. I have done much, much worse with Cappadocians, Dracul &amp; Salubri among others, believe me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lynceus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454935-methuselahs-in-the-new-world?p=1454948#post1454948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if we're saying that since Critias is based on one of Plato's students, and the legend of Atlantis comes from the dialogues of Critias and Timaeus, wherein which Critias tells the tale of Solon's journey to Egypt (where Solon heard the tale of the lost continent), that Menele was searching for Atlantis...wow. With nothing more than the legend of a lost continent and a high level Auspex ability, he made his way to the New World That's kind of nuts, lol. But after some digging, there are unconfirmed theories that the Phoenicians made their way to the New World, so I guess that's not so farfetched.</div> </div> </div> </div>Curiously, while it might have been pretty awesome, the writers of Chicago by Night seen to utterly ignore the Critias - Atlantis - New World angle.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:rubik\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">(As an aside, in my own games Critias, while officially supporting the Caine mythos for the sake of politics,</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:rubik\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> is secretly</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:rubik\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> one of the leading exponents of a blood cult that advocates vampires come <b>not </b>from Caine or Lilith, but the Antediluvians are the founding kings and queens of Atlantis, the semidivine children of the &quot;God of the Abyss&quot;, that might be Poseidon, Okeanos, Nereus, Pontus or somebody else altogether. Timaeus is his childe and the main leader of the mediterranean branch, from his domain in Tunis) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Menele's backstory speaks of &quot;phoenician legends&quot; apparently confirming my &quot;lost punic traveler chronicles&quot; angle while Critias' mentions that he financed &quot;a secret sea voyage by a captain that wanted to confirm the world was round&quot; in 1415 while in Barcelona and how the captain was never seen again, implying <b>that</b> was the precise date of Menele's trip.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:rubik\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">That said, the fact it </span></span></span><i>might </i><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:rubik\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">be the one doesn't it </span></span></span><b>has </b><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:rubik\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">to be the precise ship Menele took - world is a big place and the ship could have disappeared for a number of other reasons unrelated to Critias' sire, whom he hasn't (knowingly) seen in millenia. Considering one of the motives for Menele to try to fake Final Death was how, </span></span></span><i>about 12 centuries after Pompeii's destruction</i><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:rubik\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">, Prias had started to become a serious factor in unbalancing the dispute in Helena's favor, so any time between 1200-1415 should be acceptable for STs who want him to have more time in the Americas.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:rubik\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lynceus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454935-methuselahs-in-the-new-world?p=1454948#post1454948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if we are saying The Slumbering Giant came across the land bridge, what about the Nosferatu Methuselah that Mictlantecuhtli commited Diablerie upon? They must have found their way to South America in what, the 6th century? Who also, apparently, was fleeing the Jyhad.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <br /> That Nosferatu is kind of a complicated case in a number of ways - the fact he wasn't running away from the Jyhad per se, but trying to bring Mictlan <i>into it</i> for one, the later coming of the concept of the Nictuku as a thing for another, among some tidbits. Also, his actual generation might be far more questionable than people give credit for, since Mictlan with time become something of a diablerie connoisseur and a master thaumaturgist that created (at least) two rituals that can mess with Generation or Diablerie effectiveness.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lynceus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454935-methuselahs-in-the-new-world?p=1454948#post1454948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:rubik\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">I don't know what's more amazing- that multiple 4th Generation vampires got the idea to head to the New World, or that they made it without going &quot;ah, you know what, this is a terrible idea&quot;.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, not crazier than actual human beings that did the same <b>without</b> the help of centuries or millenia of experience and a boatload of disciplines. Remember how Alaska first enters history books as a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alaska#Colonization\" target=\"_blank\">russian</a> possession? Or how far Alexander the Great's war campaigns <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_the_Great#Revolt_of_the_army\" target=\"_blank\">went</a>? (According to the books, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Petaniqua\" target=\"_blank\">his mom</a> became Malkavian - or Baali - by the way) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Who's to say some subject of his most easterly <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wars_of_the_Diadochi\" target=\"_blank\">sucessors</a>, or some of the states that came after then didn't make that foray long before the cossacks?<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, just to shake things some more, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ocean_current\" target=\"_blank\">here </a>is a little something bound to help spark anachronistic geographical shenanigans for fun &amp; profit of one's games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-28-2022, 05:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-15T11:19:26-07:00","id":1454983,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the replies, I do think it's interesting that they bothered to use the historical figure of Critias and then never bothered to include the main reason why he's remembered to this day. Then again, they totally changed the relationship between Menele and Helena for their own purposes as well. I really like your idea that Atlantis is the origin of the Kindred, it's a neat concept, though I'm not sure how you could implement it in most Chronicles other than &quot;yeah there's a secret society of vampires who believe THIS&quot;. Still cool though!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-15T11:44:58-07:00","id":1454984,"title":"","content":"Obviously some of this is simply a matter of personal taste. If you don't like it, then it seems silly. If you do like it, it adds another layer of mystery. The idea of certain vampires making their way from the Old World to the New World isn't any crazier than all the real world theories of pre-Columbian contact (some of which are silly, some are plausible but without evidence, and others unlikely but very cool).<br /> <br /> We can divide these into several groups.<br /> <br /> The first are ancient vampires who seem to have crossed the Bering Strait. I would include all the vampires described in Diablerie Mexico here - the Slumbering Giant and the unnamed Nosferatu. Their clans (Gangrel and Nosferatu) are the ones established as the most likely to survive in the wilderness so it isn't much of a surprise that some could find their way to the Americas. Both could easily have reasons for wanting to flee and having come to a remote spot on the Chukchi Peninsula realized there was something on the other side (perhaps as a result of Auspex, an occult vision, pure guesswork, or anything else you see fit). This was a very early sourcebook so intentionally including these vampires here could have been a way to allow STs to have their own small, secret lineages of these clans if they wanted.<br /> <br /> Menele's voyage to the New World is in a different category. He fled across the Atlantic Ocean only a relatively short time before Columbus. This would have occurred at a time when the Europeans knew well that the world was round and that they were just beginning to have maritime technology capable of surviving such a voyage. As long as we accept that Menele somehow knew that there was land overseas (through some occult means available to him as an ancient vampire), then it is feasible for him to have arranged it. And as to the dangers of sailing the ocean, simply having a power like Weather Control or Auspex (to detect storms before they happen), such dangers could be reduced heavily. After all, these vampires just wants to get here, they don't care about the poor mortals who have to make their way back (and likely don't want them to). Again, CbN was one of the first sourcebooks for Vampire, so we know this was one of the original conceits of the game. One thing that does surprise me, is that there's never been (to my knowledge) any vampire who entered North America through the Viking settlements of Greenland and Vinland. That would fit this category of &quot;Atlantic crossing only when European shipbuilding technology became good enough&quot;.<br /> <br /> Then we have the story of the Baali Huitzilopochtli in Chaos Factor published in 1993. That doesn't fit either category. I don't have this sourcebook so I don't know the details of how he was supposed to have travelled to the New World. But depending on your depiction of the Baali and Infernalism, it could be justified through some kind of magic. 1993 is still very young in WoD publishing terms and the Baali as a concept had already been introduced in the first Storytellers Guide. So it seems to support a general idea that the creators of the game were purposefully positioning Mesoamerica as a center of vampire activity in the New World. Given that region's association with blood with human sacrifice and vampire bats, it makes a thematic sense. But it still seems unclear to me how the Baali reached there. Given nothing else, I'd likely put it as a result of the fabled navigations of the Phoenicians and Carthaginians making them a third point of possible contact. We know these peoples were skilled navigators and there are unproven theories of possible Phoenician contact with the Americas. That's interesting enough pseudohistory for me to say it could happen in the WoD. And it works better than the other two contact points. Furthermore if there were vampires who transited to the New World at this time, it gives credence to Menele finding such records and convincing him to make the voyage as well a thousand or more years later.<br /> <br /> The Tlacique are more problematic because they weren't an original part of the World of Darkness, but a late edition in the Revised era, presumably to help expand the Setites. As such, they are a late addition to canon and don't fit into the original intentions of the game's creators. Rather than make yet another origin point for their arrival in the Americas, it would make better sense that they came from one of the established points, like the presumed Phoenician/Carthaginian point of contact. That lends itself to the idea that the Tlacique were part of the Baali transfer to Mesoamerica. Or perhaps pursued them to the Americas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-15T13:36:58-07:00","id":1454989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454935-methuselahs-in-the-new-world?p=1454984#post1454984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that does surprise me, is that there's never been (to my knowledge) any vampire who entered North America through the Viking settlements of Greenland and Vinland. That would fit this category of &quot;Atlantic crossing only when European shipbuilding technology became good enough&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Bjorn_Garinson\" target=\"_blank\">Bjorn Garinson</a> from DC by Night, while not a part of Leif Erikson's crew per se, had heard stories about Vinland and decided to make the journey with a group of reavers due to the growing <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christianization_of_Scandinavia\" target=\"_blank\">christianization of Scandinavia</a>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454935-methuselahs-in-the-new-world?p=1454984#post1454984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then we have the story of the Baali Huitzilopochtli in Chaos Factor published in 1993. That doesn't fit either category. I don't have this sourcebook so I don't know the details of how he was supposed to have travelled to the New World. But depending on your depiction of the Baali and Infernalism, it could be justified through some kind of magic. 1993 is still very young in WoD publishing terms and the Baali as a concept had already been introduced in the first Storytellers Guide. So it seems to support a general idea that the creators of the game were purposefully positioning Mesoamerica as a center of vampire activity in the New World. Given that region's association with blood with human sacrifice and vampire bats, it makes a thematic sense. But it still seems unclear to me how the Baali reached there. Given nothing else, I'd likely put it as a result of the fabled navigations of the Phoenicians and Carthaginians making them a third point of possible contact. We know these peoples were skilled navigators and there are unproven theories of possible Phoenician contact with the Americas. That's interesting enough pseudohistory for me to say it could happen in the WoD. And it works better than the other two contact points. Furthermore if there were vampires who transited to the New World at this time, it gives credence to Menele finding such records and convincing him to make the voyage as well a thousand or more years later.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll have to reread the damn thing to be sure, but if memory tricks me not Chaos Factor gives little to no detail on how Shaitan/Huitlzilopochtli ended in Mexico or reasons beyond &quot;for the evulz&quot;. I <i>think </i>Mexico City by Night does some effort of expanding/retconing/updating Huitlzil's, so that might be another book worth checking out for those with an interest on the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-15T14:47:20-07:00","id":1454993,"title":"","content":"Black Fox largely covered what I was gonna say but I basically agree, while I do think that having old world elders in the new world (terms used for sake of simplicity, imperfect as they are) is overused and often bizarre and/or a blatant excuse to have super powerful characters in a city that\u2019s a quarter of that character\u2019s age.<br /> <br /> I do tend to think though that the early vampires should have ended up basically wherever humans did, following them all the way, maybe with some unique bloodlines sprouting up here and there. I usually run that most new world cities do have some fairly venerable vampires of indigenous origin scattered around, either in torpor or rising from it, but that the majority of pre-Colombian vampires were destroyed in the apocalyptic catastrophe that was suddenly having the human populations you feed from decimate and the introduction of new vampires (often ones capable of influencing the actions of the settler-colonizers they\u2019re traveling with) who have an ideological and religious motivation to hunt you for your heart\u2019s blood.<br /> <br /> Which isn\u2019t to say that their aren\u2019t still pre-Colombian dynasties of American vampires, but that like the indigenous people of the Americas, they\u2019ve become outnumbered by the transplants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-15T15:02:18-07:00","id":1454994,"title":"","content":"I still think the Tlacique could be a Drowned Legacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-15T16:57:09-07:00","id":1454996,"title":"","content":"I know what they said Mesoamerican and South American are two very different cultures but so are European and Middle Eastern and they both have Cainites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-16T15:09:48-07:00","id":1455044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454935-methuselahs-in-the-new-world?p=1454993#post1454993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Black Fox largely covered what I was gonna say but I basically agree, while I do think that having old world elders in the new world (terms used for sake of simplicity, imperfect as they are) is overused and often bizarre and/or a blatant excuse to have super powerful characters in a city that\u2019s a quarter of that character\u2019s age.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, writers love making NPCs and not having a city's age or paucity of materials in the history of a region before the city limit them. People can move between places during their lives, centuries old undead bloodsuckers even more so, might guess. No big deal there.<br /> <br /> What I do think is the actual issue that is a tendency of the fanbase tends to conflate/confuse NPC numbers with setting facts, to be honest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454935-methuselahs-in-the-new-world?p=1454993#post1454993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do tend to think though that the early vampires should have ended up basically wherever humans did, following them all the way, maybe with some unique bloodlines sprouting up here and there. I usually run that most new world cities do have some fairly venerable vampires of indigenous origin scattered around, either in torpor or rising from it, but that the majority of pre-Colombian vampires were destroyed in the apocalyptic catastrophe that was suddenly having the human populations you feed from decimate and the introduction of new vampires (often ones capable of influencing the actions of the settler-colonizers they\u2019re traveling with) who have an ideological and religious motivation to hunt you for your heart\u2019s blood.<br /> <br /> Which isn\u2019t to say that their aren\u2019t still pre-Colombian dynasties of American vampires, but that like the indigenous people of the Americas, they\u2019ve become outnumbered by the transplants.</div> </div> </div> </div>They do. Mictlan was embraced in what would one day become British Columbia in the same decade Caesar was invading Gaul - and yet his backstory mentions how he come across <i>other </i>vampires during his travels, how they formed cliques of their own and he mostly prefered to keep his distance from them. Not to mention one notable incident where he tried to join a tribe and start a new &quot;mortal&quot; life - only to be almost destroyed <i>because everybody was familiar with vampires and quickly started a posse to hunt him down</i> after one or two nights.<br /> <br /> Not to mention the &quot;mystery Nosferatu&quot; coming after Mictlan <b><i>because he heard many stories about him</i></b> and got curious - and the Gangrel never left the Americas.<br /> <br /> So, pretty good hints in Diablerie: Mexico of there already being a respectable number of native vampires doing exactly the same crap to humanity in the Americas they did in Europe, Middle East and other places, from 2000 to 1500 years (about the time he entered voluntary torpor) ago.<br /> <br /> Just a matter of there not being many more canon NPCs in the books to highlight that. A bit of a spot where the writers intention to &quot;keep things mysterious&quot; turned at least a little against them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454935-methuselahs-in-the-new-world?p=1454994#post1454994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still think the Tlacique could be a Drowned Legacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely see no issue with that either way. Maybe they are, maybe they are not. Could be a curious case of inversion, where they are 100% native but see the Setites as a branch that made the jump to Africa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-28-2022, 05:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-17T05:55:55-07:00","id":1455073,"title":"","content":"I'd expect Lasombra methuselahs to get around. If any kindred are going to migrate through the depths of the oceans, it's the Gangrel or them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454935-methuselahs-in-the-new-world?p=1454996#post1454996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know what they said Mesoamerican and South American are two very different cultures but so are European and Middle Eastern and they both have Cainites.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more a matter of logistics than culture, depending on when and where the first Cainites existed and how and why they travelled. A similar topic is raised in <i>Mummy: The Curse</i>, which features mummies all over the world, in spite of all them having lived at a specific place and time in pre-dynastic Egypt. One could also ask why so many of the methuselahs that we know of are in Europe as opposed to western Asia.<br /> <br /> Whereas the Europe and the MIddle East, depending on where exactly you draw the borders, are next to each other. And lot of European culture originated in the Middle East anyway. That's why we sometimes call Mesopotamia &quot;the cradle of civilisation&quot;. It isn't the cradle of <i>all</i> civilisation of course, including pre-Columbian American cultures, but it's very significant to Europe.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-17T06:06:09-07:00","id":1455074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454935-methuselahs-in-the-new-world?p=1455073#post1455073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd expect Lasombra methuselahs to get around. If any kindred are going to migrate through the depths of the oceans, it's the Gangrel or them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It's more a matter of logistics than culture, depending on when and where the first Cainites existed and how and why they travelled. A similar topic is raised in <i>Mummy: The Curse</i>, which features mummies all over the world, in spite of all them having lived at a specific place and time in pre-dynastic Egypt. One could also ask why so many of the methuselahs that we know of are in Europe as opposed to western Asia.<br /> <br /> Whereas the Europe and the MIddle East, depending on where exactly you draw the borders, are next to each other. And lot of European culture originated in the Middle East anyway. That's why we sometimes call Mesopotamia &quot;the cradle of civilisation&quot;. It isn't the cradle of <i>all</i> civilisation of course, including pre-Columbian American cultures, but it's very significant to Europe.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but Mesoamerica and South America are right next to each other too. It\u2019s not impossible that the Drowned Legacies could have spread north into Mexico.<br /> <br /> Anyway. This point is tangential to the main thread so imma drop it for now. Thanks for answering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-17T11:01:51-07:00","id":1455080,"title":"","content":"Writers, and historians for that matter, tend to write about things that are interesting. The &quot;completely normal&quot; isn't that interesting. This makes it seem like a bias where you've got so much emphasis on the few Methuselahs shown off in the new world and nobody writes about the presumed myriad of Methuselahs chilling in the middle east (there are of course, other factors like familiarity, but this is a pretty big one.)<br /> <br /> there's this perception that people in early-modern england emptied their chamberpots out the window, pooring their shit on the street. In reality, that happened a few times, it was newsworthy, and people were very angry at the fool who threw their shit out the window. Most people would take such waste to the downstream part of the river or give it to the people who process this stuff (it's chiefly great for tanning, fertilizer, and gunpowder). But somehow, the exceptions to the rule became sensationalized and now most have this idea that throwing shit out of the window was normal (This was kinda aided by victorian-era historians wanting to make the past barbaric so their own era seemed better). <br /> <br /> Point being, most princes likely have fairly stable domains, they rule well, and vampire plots take years to achieve. But for the purposes of Drama we need shitty, awful princes with domains on the verge of anarchy. We need methuselahs in the USA because they're interesting and the US is unstable, but we also want some ancient methuselahs that came to the USA well before they really should have because it's intriguing to have methuselah from pre-urbanization of the USA; that helps reinforce how ancient and unfathomable they are. <br /> <br /> In-universe? I'd say Methuselahs moved over because they were the losers or were otherwise threatened and felt the best thing to do would be to create some distance. Perhaps they spent a lot of time flying around the globe with astral projection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-18T16:43:07-07:00","id":1455137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454935-methuselahs-in-the-new-world?p=1454941#post1454941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wanderer, assuming you mean Mictlantecuhtli, was indigenous, so it's more a question of how/why his sire was in the Americas. A Gangrel Methuselah is probably the best equipped to make such a journey on their own (assuming they actually are Gangrel).<br /> <br /> In Menele's case, my understanding is that he took the journey with no question &quot;if&quot; there was another continent (I thought he knew due to advanced Auspex, but wiki says he was motivated by ancient legends, which does seem a bit sketchier). A journey that might be dangerous for mortals would probably be less so for a Methuselah in possession of advanced Thaumaturgy.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I don't see a reason the Gangrel and other vampires couldn't have come over the Land Bridge. Vampires follow their food.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-18T19:08:58-07:00","id":1455155,"title":"","content":"Assuming that vampirism dates as close to the origin of Man as vampires themselves believe, then it certainly follows that they would have come to the Americas along with the first human beings to do so in ancient antiquity.<br /> <br /> Characters from the Trojan War turning up in the American midwest? That's Mark Rein\u2022Hagen and Jonathan Tweet setting their game in the region where they grew up so they could write what they know. And we can tap dance and try to make it make sense within the game's fictional history, but ultimately it's something really pedestrian and human and understandable happening at the author level. And I kind of love it for what it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-18T20:48:27-07:00","id":1455164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454935-methuselahs-in-the-new-world?p=1455155#post1455155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming that vampirism dates as close to the origin of Man as vampires themselves believe, then it certainly follows that they would have come to the Americas along with the first human beings to do so in ancient antiquity.<br /> <br /> Characters from the Trojan War turning up in the American midwest? That's Mark Rein\u2022Hagen and Jonathan Tweet setting their game in the region where they grew up so they could write what they know. And we can tap dance and try to make it make sense within the game's fictional history, but ultimately it's something really pedestrian and human and understandable happening at the author level. And I kind of love it for what it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hate that Menele was a &quot;White God&quot; of the Aztecs but honestly, I do like that 1st Edition made it clear that this kind of internationalism is common among the Kindred. Chicago had a Muslim Medieval General (Khalid), African Elder (Inyanga), and Vietnamese drug lord.<br /> <br /> It wasn't perfect but the assumption was that ancient vampires move around when their power bases collapse and the Jyhad is more a reshuffling.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-18T23:46:59-07:00","id":1455175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454935-methuselahs-in-the-new-world?p=1455137#post1455137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, I don't see a reason the Gangrel and other vampires couldn't have come over the Land Bridge. Vampires follow their food.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely agree, as the first part of my post indicated. I was just teasing at the idea of it being a native bloodline that had a lot in common with the Gangrel Clan instead, especially since it was relatively early in the series when the Wanderer and his sire were written, before groups like the Laibon were added.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-19T14:33:47-07:00","id":1455215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454935-methuselahs-in-the-new-world?p=1455080#post1455080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In-universe? I'd say Methuselahs moved over because they were the losers or were otherwise threatened and felt the best thing to do would be to create some distance. Perhaps they spent a lot of time flying around the globe with astral projection.</div> </div> </div> </div>This also is exactly why Menele fled to the New World. He was losing against Helena. He faked his death and fled somewhere he thought she'd never follow. The journey to the Americas assuredly seemed dangerous, but staying in the Old World seemed even more dangerous.<br /> <br /> Same reason Nergal fled to the Americas, too. The Baali were regarded as a pox by other Kindred and Nergal and his followers especially. Everyone hated them. The New World seemed like a good place to hide. <br /> <br /> Some vampires, like the Gangrel, might have crossed the ocean out of wanderlust. But for the most part, vampires who are doing fine and peachy where they are don't get up and leave. Distant lands filled with unknowable dangers and few apparent opportunities are going to attract losers rather than winners in the Jyhad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-19T15:57:31-07:00","id":1455219,"title":"","content":"I think that's an insightful answer. You're right, whether starting over represents a setback or a needed opportunity says everything about how someone has been doing so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-19T18:11:47-07:00","id":1455223,"title":"","content":"Mind you, 4th generation vampires don't have to worry about Kine concerns. 8th through 13th vampires will probably only encounter ghosts and the occasional werewolf.<br /> <br /> 4th?<br /> <br /> 4th can have a bunch of sidhe boatsmiths and mages build them a ship from Middle Earth to take them across a bridge of rainbows to America.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}